From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:27:11 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): local judges fail safe on fetched code and
 small windows

With a local judge, smart approval (provenance, 0077) allowed a subagent to run pytest in a repo it had cloned this session, even when only the parent agent claimed the user's approval. The model call and the parse were fine: qwen3-coder:30b and qwen3.5:2b answer a clean <block>no</block> at stage 1 for running, installing or building any session clone (the same for a plain chat with no subagent), and qwen3-coder:30b at stage 2 allows it too, calling the clone trusted or crediting the parent's relayed claim. They do block curl | sh and an injected force push, which is all the earlier differential tested.

The review now finds, from the session's finished terminal calls (the root chat's and the subagent's), the paths it cloned (git clone, gh repo clone), unpacked (tar -C, unzip -d) or downloaded (curl -o, wget -O). A command that runs in or names such a path carries it as the harness fact runs_in_session_fetch, skips stage 1 and goes to stage 2. A self-hosted stage-2 judge's allow on it becomes unsure, which asks the user; a hosted judge's allow stands. The review prompt itself is unchanged: one sentence describing the new fact made qwen3-coder:30b allow two injected force pushes at stage 2 that it blocks without it. A command that upstream's dangerous-command patterns flag (curl | sh, a force push) also skips stage 1, since qwen3.5:2b allows curl | sh there.

A self-hosted judge (Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM, also when the review follows the main model's server) is checked against the window it is served with. A prompt larger than that window is not sent, and a reply whose prompt token count shows the server cut the prompt is not used: either way the verdict is unsure with the reason logged, so the rules never silently fall off the front. A stage-1 reply with both verdicts counts as unreadable and runs stage 2, as an empty or unreadable one already did.
